<title>USA: Utah approves measure to guarantee school debt.</title>
<headline>Utah approves measure to guarantee school debt.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Utah voters on Tuesday approved by a wide margin an amendment to the state constitution that gives the sate authority to guarantee the debt of school districts, election returns show.</p>
<p>The measure was approved 62 percent to 38 percent. It allows the state to guarantee the general obligation of every school district by providing exemptions to constitutional provisions that prohibit the state from lending its credit or assuming the debt of any school district.</p>
</text>
